---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faq = [
	{
		question: 'What is the difference between a wet alarm valve and a deluge valve?',
		answer: 'A wet alarm valve (ZSFZ) is installed in wet-pipe sprinkler systems where the piping is always charged with water; it detects flow caused by a sprinkler head opening and triggers the alarm. A deluge valve (ZSFM) is a dry control valve used in deluge systems that open to flood the entire protected area with water simultaneously — typically for high-hazard occupancies such as chemical plants and power stations.'
	},
	{
		question: 'When should a pre-action system (ZSFY) be used?',
		answer: 'Pre-action systems (ZSFY) combine a deluge-type valve with automatic sprinklers and require two independent triggers (e.g. smoke detection plus heat) before water enters the piping. They are specified for water-sensitive environments such as museums, archives, data centres and cold storage, where accidental discharge must be avoided.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What does a water flow indicator (ZSJZ) do in a sprinkler system?',
		answer: 'A vane water flow indicator (ZSJZ) is installed on sprinkler branch lines and detects water flow caused by an opened sprinkler head, sending a signal to the fire alarm panel to identify the zone of activation. It has an adjustable time delay to filter out transient pressure surges.'
	},
	{
		question: 'Are ZSFZ, ZSFM and ZSFY valves interchangeable?',
		answer: 'No. Each valve type is matched to a specific system architecture: ZSFZ for wet systems, ZSFM for deluge systems, and ZSFY for pre-action systems. Substituting one for another will break the system logic and may fail code inspection. Select according to the occupancy hazard class and the design basis.'
	},
	{
		question: 'What certifications are required for sprinkler alarm valves?',
		answer: 'Sprinkler alarm valve assemblies should be listed by the applicable approval body for your market — commonly UL/FM for North America, CE for Europe, LPCB for UK/Commonwealth projects, plus ISO 9001 as the quality baseline. Wanlian supplies ZSFZ/ZSFM/ZSFY assemblies with certification packages matched to the destination market.'
	}
];

const valveProducts = [
	{
		slug: 'wet-alarm-check-valve-zsfz-150',
		name: 'Wet Alarm Check Valve (ZSFZ-150)',
		img: 'https://s.alicdn.com/@sc04/kf/H82d57eb132e942ecba6023697838d6afn/Water-Alarm-Valves-ZSFZ-150-Flexible-Cast.png?hasNWGrade=1',
		desc: 'Wet-pipe alarm valve with flow detection and alarm trip'
	},
	{
		slug: 'deluge-alarm-valve-zsfm',
		name: 'Deluge Alarm Valve Group (ZSFM Series)',
		img: 'https://s.alicdn.com/@sc04/kf/HTB1q4J9bEzrK1RjSspm763OdFXa1.png?v=20260729',
		desc: 'Diaphragm-operated deluge valve for high-hazard occupancy'
	},
	{
		slug: 'pre-action-alarm-system-zsfy',
		name: 'Pre-action Deluge Alarm System (ZSFY Series)',
		img: 'https://s.alicdn.com/@sc04/kf/H2857379540b7417c83f169d67ff70ab3a.png_300x300.jpg?v=20260729',
		desc: 'Dual-trigger failsafe pre-action valve for water-sensitive zones'
	},
	{
		slug: 'water-flow-indicator-zsjz',
		name: 'Vane Type Water Flow Indicator (ZSJZ Series)',
		img: 'https://sc02.alicdn.com/kf/A463ac39a948d44a391017ca222837de2B.png?v=20260729',
		desc: 'Zone flow detection with adjustable delay for wet sprinklers'
	}
];
---

<Layout
	title="Fire Sprinkler System Valves: A Complete Guide (Wet, Deluge & Pre-action)"
	description="Complete guide to fire sprinkler system valves: ZSFZ wet alarm valve, ZSFM deluge valve, ZSFY pre-action system and ZSJZ water flow indicator — how each works and when to specify it."
	type="article"
	faq={faq}
>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 mb-16">
		<nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 flex gap-2">
			<a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
			<span>/</span>
			<span class="text-gray-600">Guides</span>
		</nav>

		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Fire Sprinkler System Guide</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">Fire Sprinkler System Valves: A Complete Guide (Wet, Deluge &amp; Pre-action)</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">Every sprinkler system is built around a control valve assembly — the point where the water supply becomes the fire suppression system. Specify the wrong valve type and the entire system logic fails inspection. This guide explains the four valve types that dominate modern fire sprinkler design, what each one does, and the occupancy types they protect.</p>

			<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
				{valveProducts.map(p => (
					<a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden hover:border-brand-red hover:shadow-md transition">
						<img src={p.img} alt={p.name} loading="lazy" class="w-full h-28 object-contain bg-white p-2" />
						<div class="p-3">
							<p class="text-xs font-bold text-gray-800 group-hover:text-brand-red leading-snug transition-colors">{p.name}</p>
							<p class="text-[10px] text-gray-400 mt-1 line-clamp-2">{p.desc}</p>
						</div>
					</a>
				))}
			</div>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">1. Wet-Pipe Systems: The ZSFZ Wet Alarm Valve</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Wet-pipe systems are the most common sprinkler configuration: the piping is permanently charged with water, and each sprinkler head opens individually when its heat-sensitive element bursts. The <a href="/products/wet-alarm-check-valve-zsfz-150/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZSFZ wet alarm check valve</a> sits at the system riser and performs two duties: it prevents reverse flow from the system back into the supply, and it detects the water flow created when a head opens, tripping the mechanical and electrical alarms. Flow continues into the system until the supply is shut off manually.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Wet systems are fast, simple and cheap to maintain — but they cannot be used where ambient temperatures risk freezing the piping.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">2. Deluge Systems: The ZSFM Deluge Valve</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Deluge systems protect high-hazard occupancies where fire can spread faster than individual sprinkler heads can respond: chemical plants, paint shops, power stations, aircraft hangars. All nozzles in a deluge zone are open, and the system is held back by a single control valve — the <a href="/products/deluge-alarm-valve-zsfm/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZSFM deluge alarm valve</a>. When a detection system (smoke/heat/flame) signals a fire, the valve opens and water floods every nozzle simultaneously.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">The diaphragm-operated ZSFM opens fast and reseals reliably after operation, which matters because deluge zones are often large and the valve is the single point of failure in the system.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">3. Pre-Action Systems: The ZSFY Dual-Trigger Valve</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Pre-action systems are deluge hardware with a sprinkler-pipe twist: the piping is dry, and water only enters <em>after two independent triggers confirm a fire</em>. The <a href="/products/pre-action-alarm-system-zsfy/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZSFY pre-action alarm system</a> is the control assembly for this architecture — a deluge-type valve operated by a fire detection signal, with automatic sprinklers downstream that also act as individual fuses.</p>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Why specify pre-action? Three reasons dominate:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-4">
				<li><strong>Water-sensitive contents</strong> — museums, archives, data centres, transformer rooms: no water enters unless two signals confirm.</li>
				<li><strong>Freezing environments</strong> — cold storage, unheated warehouses: dry piping cannot freeze.</li>
				<li><strong>False-discharge insurance</strong> — the dual-trigger logic makes accidental discharge statistically negligible.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">4. Zone Detection: The ZSJZ Water Flow Indicator</h2>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Once the system is operating, the fire brigade and the building manager need to know <em>which zone</em> is flowing. The <a href="/products/water-flow-indicator-zsjz/" class="text-brand-blue font-semibold hover:underline">ZSJZ vane water flow indicator</a> installs on sprinkler branch lines: when water moves, the vane deflects and the switch sends a signal to the alarm panel identifying the affected zone. An adjustable time delay filters out pressure surges that would otherwise cause nuisance alarms.</p>

			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight">5. Selecting the Right Valve for Your Project</h2>
			<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 my-5">
				<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm">
					<thead class="bg-gray-50">
						<tr>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Occupancy / Need</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">System type</th>
							<th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-bold text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Control valve</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Offices, retail, warehouses (heated)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Wet-pipe</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ZSFZ wet alarm valve</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Chemical, power, aviation, high hazard</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Deluge</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ZSFM deluge valve</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Museums, data centres, cold storage</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">Pre-action</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ZSFY pre-action system</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-gray-900">Zone identification (all wet systems)</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">—</td>
							<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-700">ZSJZ flow indicator</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A complete assembly typically pairs the alarm valve with a signal gate valve upstream, a check valve, gauges and the alarm trim. When you send us your hazard class and pipe size, we quote the full valve assembly rather than a single valve — one certified package, one set of documents.</p>

			<!-- FAQ Section -->
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-12 mb-6 tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
			<div class="space-y-4">
				{faq.map(item => (
					<details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 p-5 open:border-brand-red/30">
						<summary class="flex justify-between items-center font-bold text-gray-800 cursor-pointer list-none">
							<span>{item.question}</span>
							<span class="text-brand-blue text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
						</summary>
						<p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm">{item.answer}</p>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>

			<!-- CTA -->
			<div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
				<div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-blue to-blue-800 px-6 sm:px-10 py-10 text-center">
					<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Need a Sprinkler Valve Assembly Quoted?</h2>
					<p class="mt-3 text-blue-100 max-w-xl mx-auto text-sm leading-relaxed">Send your system type, hazard class and pipe size — we reply with the complete valve assembly spec and factory price within 12 hours.</p>
					<div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-center gap-4">
						<a href="/contact/?product=Sprinkler%20Valve%20Assembly" class="px-8 py-4 bg-brand-red text-white font-bold rounded-lg hover:opacity-90 transition">Request a Quote</a>
						<a href="https://wa.me/8618684324501?text=Hi%2C%20I%20need%20a%20sprinkler%20valve%20assembly%20quote" class="px-8 py-4 bg-white text-brand-blue font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
